From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8998: video subcore gdscs are HW_CTRL_TRIGGER

With the vcodec subcore clocks finally named on the venus node,
core_power_v1() enables them right after powering the subcore domains --
and trips over the HW_CTRL flag: gdsc_enable() hands the domain to
hardware the moment it powers it, nothing is requesting it yet, the
domain collapses, and video_subcore0_clk's CBCR polls "status stuck at
'off'" (-EBUSY), failing the whole probe.

The vendor never runs this window in hardware control: its
gdsc-regulator powers venus_core0/1 in software mode and only hands
gating to the video hardware after the session is up
(qcom,support-hw-trigger + regulator_set_mode at runtime).

HW_CTRL_TRIGGER is mainline's version of exactly that handshake: the
domain powers on in software mode, and venus's vcodec_domains_set_hw()
flips it to hardware control via dev_pm_genpd_set_hwmode() only after
the subcore clocks are enabled -- the same model sdm845+ videocc uses
for its vcodec gdscs.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
@@ -2564,7 +2564,7 @@
 	},
 	.parent = &video_top_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = HW_CTRL,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc video_subcore1_gdsc = {
@@ -2576,7 +2576,7 @@
 	},
 	.parent = &video_top_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = HW_CTRL,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc mdss_gdsc = {
